 "verdict": "THE FAMILY DIFFERENCE IS SPECIFIC TO r=2. The gap between the attractor model and the control is +60 points at r=2 and +4 at r=4, -4 at r=8, -6 at r=16. The control ACQUIRES an attractor at r=16 (61%) despite having none at r=2, so the large-radius attractor is a GENERIC long-context effect present in both models and is not the phenomenon that separates families. Read against the control, the model-distinguishing frozen phase exists ONLY at the two-token window the whole project uses -- so it is a property of the CONSTRUCTION. F35's boundary extends to cover it, and F58's critical point is the melting of a two-token degeneracy rather than a fact about language-model dynamics. ONE TOKEN CARRIES IT: banning '\\n' alone drops top-1 from 74% to 15% and the attractor is gone. It does NOT relocate -- the next dominant tokens sit at 15%, 13%, 9%, i.e. at the control's baseline. So the frozen phase rests on a single vocabulary entry, not a structural pull toward filler. CONTROL under ablation moves by only 6 points, so the collapse above is not an artifact of forbidding tokens.",
 "_analysis_provenance": {
  "script": "attractor_interventions.py",
  "sha256": "c70a9642579176a0d4438df3e9b3ba10af79d4ef17eabf50127b21227bc64a4c",
  "note": "sha256 of the analysis source at write time. If this does not match the file on disk, the analysis was produced by a different version of the code -- re-run it before reading the numbers (issue #38)."
 },
 "_note": "Two interventions on the low-temperature attractor, run because the observational axes were exhausted: the nine-model screen found the effect well separated at the threshold (later shown NOT to be bimodal -- see F64's correction, where a 26-model screen fills the apparent gap) and eliminated corpus (F63) and architecture (granite MoE vs dense agree within 2 points while differing 2x in width, 1.7x in depth, 16x in FFN and routing-vs-none). Radius asks whether the attractor belongs to the two-token conditioning window rather than the model -- if so, F58's critical point is a construction degeneracy and F35's boundary extends. Ablation asks whether it is one pathological vocabulary entry or a structural pull toward filler, by forbidding the dominant token in turn via the mechanism ARRule already uses for special tokens. gpt2-medium is the control: an intervention that moves it is not doing what it claims. Threshold is the screen's, not a fresh one."
}